\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar hesitant but steps back from edge.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolyn Cohn  \par \uc2 649 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2003\par 10:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 20 (Reuters) - The dollar withdrew from the previous day's record lows on the euro and three-year lows on the yen on Thursday, pausing from worries about trade disputes and capital flows, but wary of Japanese steps to curb yen gains.   \par \par \uc2  A textile trade row with China and weak U.S. capital flows data hit the dollar earlier this week, as investors fretted that the row would lead China to cut back on purchases of U.S. Treasuries and also that the U.S. administration would sanction a weaker dollar to protect exports and jobs.   \par \par \uc2  But wariness of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese authorities cushioned the dollar's decline on Thursday, following suspected heavy official sales of yen in the previous session.   \par \par \uc2  "There has been quite a bit of negative news for the dollar in the past few days - the trade situation suggests the Bush administration is being quite protectionist, which is not doing the dollar any favours," said Ian Stannard, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas.   \par \par \uc2  "We need to watch U.S. asset markets closely, and the Philly Fed survey today is going to be closely watched."   \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 108.91/96 yen at 0815 GMT, down a third of a percent on the day but more than one percent above three-year lows around 107.50 set on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2  The euro rose a quarter cent against the dollar to around $1.1920, more than half a cent below Wednesday's record high.   \par \par \uc2  PHILLY FED   \par \par \uc2  U.S. weekly jobless claims, due at 1330 GMT, are forecast at 365,0000 from the previous 366,000.   \par \par \uc2  The Philadelphia Federal Reserve business activity survey for November was due out at 1700 GMT. Analysts polled by Reuters expected a median reading of 25.5 versus October's 28.0.   \par \par \uc2  Federal Reserve chairman Alan Greenspan was due to speak on the current account and the euro at 1400 GMT in Washington, while ECB president Jean-Claude Trichet was scheduled to speak at 1900 GMT.   \par \par \uc2  "If Greenspan's comments suggest the dollar needs to weaken, that could cause quite a substantial decline, but then Trichet might caution over euro strength," said Adrian Schmidt, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at RBS Financial Markets.   \par \par \uc2  French third quarter gross domestic product rose by 0.4 percent on the quarter while German third quarter GDP was confirmed at a rise of 0.2 percent in the third quarter.   \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) council holds a regular meeting on Thursday but was not due to discuss monetary policy.   \par \par \uc2  U.S. stocks rose after four straight losing sessions on Wednesday and futures were indicating a flat to higher open on Wall Street, but U.S. Treasury prices weakened.   \par \par \uc2  Analysts said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market scandal in the United States was dampening sentiment but having little direct \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  impact.   \par \par \uc2  Federal authorities on Wednesday charged 47 people with running a scam in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market that defrauded retail investors and big Wall Street firms of millions of dollars.   \par \par \uc2  SELLING YEN   \par \par \uc2  The Japanese authorities were believed to have stepped into the market on Wednesday immediately after the yen touched multi-year highs against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2  Traders in Tokyo estimated Japanese authorities sold around 800 billion yen ($7.3 billion) for dollars.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent about 16 trillion yen on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first 10 months of the year on concerns that its export-reliant economic recovery would be choked off by a further rise in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  Japan's overall trade surplus for October rose 20.4 percent from a year earlier to 1.0739 trillion yen ($9.83 billion).   \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar was steady near the previous day's six-year highs, shrugging off data from the Reserve Bank of Australia showing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a larger-than-usual amount A$1.772 billion in October.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031120dzbk002gu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
