\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar weak, eyes record lows vs euro.  \b0\par\par\uc2 550 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2003\par 08:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Reuters offers a scrolling news service for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  professionals who want to follow market developments minute by minute. Click here for the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  news and views  \par \par \uc2 By Naomi Tajitsu  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Nov 20 (Reuters) - The dollar was softer on Thursday on geopolitical concerns and worries about the U.S. economy, eroding gains it had made a day earlier from record lows against the euro and three-year troughs against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Still, wariness of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese authorities cushioned the decline, keeping trading in relatively narrow ranges.  \par \par \uc2 "I would not say it is falling (against both the euro and yen) anymore. Movement has become much more horizontal," said Mitsuru Sahara, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at UFJ Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "There is not a lot of selling going on," he said. "They (traders) are afraid of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was at 108.91/96 at 0626 GMT, down by more than a quarter yen on the day against the Japanese unit and almost 1.4 percent off three-year lows around 107.50 set on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The euro rose a quarter cent against the dollar to around $1.1916/22 about a half cent off Wednesday's record high of $1.1978.  \par \par \uc2 The conflict in Iraq and worries about the fallout from Washington's plans to impose import quotas on Chinese textiles continued to plague the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the Japanese authorities were believed to have stepped into the market immediately after the yen touched multi-year highs against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 A report in the Nihon Keizai Shimbun financial daily said that Japan sold an estimated one trillion yen ($9.16 billion) for dollars.  \par \par \uc2 JAPANESE EXPORTS  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent about 16 trillion yen on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first 10 months of the year on concerns that its export-reliant economic recovery would be choked off by a further rise in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  revealed on Thursday that Japan's overall trade surplus for October rose 20.4 percent from a year earlier to 1.0739 trillion yen ($9.83 billion).  \par \par \uc2 Peter Morgan, chief economist at HSBC Securities Japan, said the current exchange rate levels don't seem to be inflicting much damage to Japan's export economy.  \par \par \uc2 "The current level is still okay. If it breaks through 100 (yen to the dollar), it's more of a significant problem," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's persistent trade surplus was a yen-boosting factor in itself as Japanese exporters convert dollars earned overseas into yen.  \par \par \uc2 But traders said that the supply-and-demand factors on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market were not as acutely in favour of a higher yen as they were in recent months when the Nikkei share average was marching higher.  \par \par \uc2 The Nikkei average rose 2.61 percent to 9,865.70 on Thursday but traders said its recent slide below the 10,000 level suggested that foreign investors, who had led the rally from 20-year lows around 7,600 set in April, were no longer aggressive buyers.  \par \par \uc2 "We will continue to see dollar-selling by exporters. But as you can see from stock prices, there isn't a great deal of inflow (to Japan)," said Masamichi Koike, head of spot \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Sumitomo Mitsui Bank. ($1=109.16 yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031120dzbk001vn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
