\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF Hayashi After Suspected  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Wed  \b0\par\par\uc2 312 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2003\par 09:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sufficient funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for now, the Japanese Finance Ministry's top bureaucrat said Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 "We have no specific plan on procuring additional funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Masakazu Hayashi, the administrative vice finance minister, told a regular press conference.  \par \par \uc2 Hayashi added that the MOF doesn't intend to ask the Bank of Japan for help in procuring additional funds to carry out \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "We won't make a request to the BOJ, but we are studying the issue," Hayashi said.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan, acting on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is estimated to have bought between $5 billion and $10 billion for yen Wednesday to help lift the dollar by around Y1.5 from a fresh 3-year low of Y107.52.  \par \par \uc2 So far in November, the ministry is suspected to have sold roughly Y2 trillion to prevent an excessively strong yen from hampering Japan's economic recovery. In October, it sold Y2.7 trillion, bringing the total amount of yen it has sold in the first 10 months of 2003 to Y16.2 trillion.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts estimate the ministry's outstanding \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  bills total Y73 trillion.  \par \par \uc2 But the ministry has an issue ceiling of Y79 trillion for the fiscal year to next March, raising concerns it may be running out of ammunition for further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The situation has spurred speculation that the ministry may ask the BOJ to buy foreign bonds via repurchase agreements from the government to provide funds for more \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Hayashi shrugged off the view, saying the ministry won't make such a request at the BOJ's two-day policy-setting meeting, which ends Friday.  \par \par \uc2 -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Hugh Lawson and Mary de Wet  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031120dzbk000f1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
