s keen to see if cleaning services company will maintain target of op margin of 5.6% to 5.7% for FY. \par  \par Cosmote (COSMO.AT): 9-Mos Earnings \par Consensus net profit (DJ, 4 analysts): EUR189M (EUR170M) \par Note: On a quarterly basis, earnings seen up 5% to EUR74M vs EUR70.7M, although 02 net profit figure may be revised. Average revenue per user will be closely monitored for future prospects. 9-Mos ARPU seen down 3% to EUR29, given the growing switch to pre-paid contracts. \par  \par Tomkins (TOMK.LN): 3Q Earnings \par Consensus operating profit before exceptionals and goodwill (Company, 7 analysts): GBP73.5M (GBP70M) \par Note: Previous year's result is an estimate as company has changed its accounting reference date to December 31 from April 30. Progress on integration of acquisitions and full-year outlook will be the focus. \par  \par SSL International (SSL.LN): 1H Earnings \par Consensus sales (DJ, analysts): GBP316 (308M) \par Note: Figures seen in line with company trading statement in Oct, say analysts who are not forecasting profit figures. Analysts want update on sale of medical unit. SSL has said it has interested buyers and will complete sale by end 2003. \par  \par VimpelCom (VIMP.RS): 3Q Earnings \par Consensus net profit (DJ, 5 analysts): USD76M (USD40M) \par Consensus sales: USD379M (USD221M) \par Forecast range: USD71M - USD82M \par Note: EBITDA called at USD178M from USD103M. "We expect improvement in revenues and the highest profit margin year-to-date (versus previous two quarters) due to high seasonal subscriber growth," Konstantin Chernyshev at Nikoil says. Elena Rogovina of Alfa Bank says "The third quarter is traditionally the best for mobile companies due to a seasonal increase in mobile usage and higher roaming revenues during the peak summer season alongside strong growth in the mobile subscriber base." \par  \par FKI Group (FKI.LN): 1H Earnings \par Consensus pretax profit (DJ, 6 analysts): GBP28.5M  (GBP44.7M) \par Forecast range: 