\par\par \b \uc2 Japan's Watanabe - Dlr moving on geopolitical factors.  \b0\par\par\uc2 277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2003\par 11:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Nov 12 (Reuters) - The dollar's recent moves were based more on geopolitical factors than on economic fundamentals, a senior Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) official said on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 "Since late Friday, the market seems to be moving more on geopolitical factors," Hiroshi Watanabe, head of the MOF's International Bureau, told reporters when asked about the impact of Japan's general elections on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 Warnings of attacks in Saudi Arabia and rumours, later denied, that the United States would raise its terror alert level had dented the dollar in late New York on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Watanabe added that movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market had been subdued in the past few days, but that authorities would continue to monitor the market closely.  \par \par \uc2 Market sources said that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York after the dollar retested three-year lows around 107.86 yen, and started bidding again on Tuesday when the dollar was near 108.65 yen.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback was trading around 108.95 late on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 MOF officials have declined to comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Watanabe added that he did not detect any major capital flows across borders and that the domestic stock market's decline was partly due to fund flows from stocks into Japanese bonds.  \par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi's three-way coalition won Sunday's general election but with a reduced majority as the main opposition Democratic Party advanced.  \par \par \uc2 On the possibility of raising the ceiling on funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Watanabe said that a decision on whether to compile a supplementary budget for the current fiscal year needed to be made first.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031112dzbc0022n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
