\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen slips after suspected  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kyle Peterson  \par \uc2 612 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2003\par 22:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Reuters offers a scrolling news service for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  professionals who want to follow market developments minute by minute. Click here for the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  news and views ) (Updates prices, adds comment)  \par \par \uc2 CHICAGO, Nov 11 (Reuters) - The dollar on Tuesday its trimmed losses from a near three-year low notched against the yen on Monday, after suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Tokyo weighed on the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 A long-standing downside bias for the dollar brought the greenback broadly lower, strategists said, noting that a period of strong U.S. economic data has come to an end without sparking a big rally and future data might not be as rosy.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. markets were mostly calm on the Veterans Day Holiday. A lack of economic data contributed to that lull and pit trade in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures at the Chicago Mercantile Exchange was closed.  \par \par \uc2 "There was a move up. It actually began before we went home yesterday. All I know is there were (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) rumors overnight," said Bob Lynch, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas in New York. "It's certainly understandable that people would expect the (Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was near flat on the day at 108.71 yen , but up from Monday's three-year low of 107.86 yen, while the euro climbed to 125.11 yen , up 0.30 percent after having dropped more than 1 percent on Monday to a 10-month low.  \par \par \uc2 "The Bank of Japan is leaning against a very strong investor flow," said David Durrant, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank Julius Baer in New York. "We look at custody data and equity investment continues to flow toward Asia," he said.  \par \par \uc2 "When you look at valuation problems at U.S. stocks and the stronger euro and worry about European companies, there is a good investor bias to continue to add to Asia exposure," Durrant added.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, said on Tuesday he could not comment on whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but said officials would not tolerate excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves. Echoing Mizoguchi, Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said the authorities would act against sudden movements.  \par \par \uc2 In addition to speculated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a 2.8 percent fall in Tokyo stocks and worse-than-expected Japanese machinery orders data, a key gauge of trends in capital spending, also weighed against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 In Europe, one piece of good news was the 16-month high in Germany's influential ZEW index of investor expectations. In September it jumped more than expected to 67.2, boosted by strong orders, a stock market rally and a weaker euro.  \par \par \uc2 "The ZEW survey was definitely positive for the euro but U.S. data have been strong so it will be difficult for the euro to make a huge amount of headway," said Mary Davis, global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at CSFB.  \par \par \uc2 Also encouraging for the euro zone was a 5.6 percent year-on-year rise in German exports in September.  \par \par \uc2 The euro rose slightly after the 