\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen off 3-yr highs on suspected  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Daniel Bases   \par \uc2 644 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2003\par 17:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds comment, changes byline, changes dateline, previous LONDON)   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Nov 11 (Reuters) - The yen slipped from three-year highs against the dollar and lost a step against the euro on Tuesday after suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Tokyo put a check against the rapid buying of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 A long-standing downside bias for the dollar brought the greenback broadly lower, strategists said, as a period of strong U.S. economic data has come to an end without sparking a big rally and future data might not be as rosy.   \par \par \uc2 With U.S. financial markets in a lull during the Veterans Day holiday and lack of data until Thursday's U.S. international trade report, trading was subdued.   \par \par \uc2 "If there was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if was probably out of concern for the speed of yen appreciation rather than direction. We are looking for dollar/yen around 107 by the end of the month," said Rebecca Patterson, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan Chase in New York.   \par \par \uc2 "Because of the U.S. holiday it is relatively quiet, but it does appear the gradual dollar downtrend remains in place. It is not that the U.S. looks horrible, but that there are potential investments outside the U.S. that have more upside," she added.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar held unchanged at 108.65 yen, up from Monday's three-year low of 107.86 yen, while the euro climbed to 125.25 yen, up 0.40 percent after having dropped over 1 percent on Monday to a 10-month low.   \par \par \uc2 "The Bank of Japan is leaning against a very strong investor flow," said David Durrant, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank Julius Baer in New York, adding, "We look at custody data and equity investment continues to flow toward Asia."   \par \par \uc2 "When you look at valuation problems at U.S. stocks and the stronger euro and worry about European companies, there is a good investor bias to continue to add to Asia exposure," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Finance Ministry officials declined to comment on whether they had stepped into the market to stem the yen's rise.   \par \par \uc2 Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, said on Tuesday he could not comment on whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but said officials would not tolerate excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves.   \par \par \uc2 Echoing Mizoguchi, Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said the authorities would act against sudden movements.   \par \par \uc2 In addition to speculated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a 2.8 percent fall in Tokyo stocks and worse-than-expected machinery orders data, a key gauge of trends in capital spending also weighing against the yen.   \par \par \uc2 Looking toward Europe, one piece of good news was the 16-month high in Germany's influential ZEW index of investor expectations. In September it jumped more than expected to 67.2, boosted by strong orders, a stock market rally and a weaker euro.   \par \par \uc2 "The ZEW survey was definitely positive for the euro but U.S. data have been strong so it will be difficult for the euro to make a huge amount of headway," said Mary Davis, global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at CSFB.   \par \par \uc2 Also encouraging for the euro zone was a 5.6 percent year-on-year rise in German exports in September.   \par \par \uc2 The euro rose slightly after the ZEW data, trading at $1.1519 per dollar, up 0.30 percent on the day and just around a cent above seven-week lows set last week.   \par \par \uc2 Among the dollar bloc, the New Zealand dollar soared to a new six-year high of US$0.6266 before slipping back to US$0.6255, a gain of 0.67 percent on the day. The rally for the kiwi was sparked by a drop in New Zealand's unemployment rate to a 15-year low in the third quarter, boosting expectations for a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest rate hike next month.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031111dzbb003aq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
