\par\par \b \uc2 TECHNICALS- \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  market views and key levels.  \b0\par\par\uc2 667 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2003\par 17:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     NEW YORK, Nov 11 (Reuters) - Following is a selection of\par comments from analysts on important technical developments in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par     TOM FITZPATRICK, CHIEF TECHNICAL ANALYST, CITIFX\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - EURO/DOLLAR: "There is consolidation between the gap  \f28 \par \par \uc2 support at $1.1390-$1.1380 and the neckline of the double top.  \par \par \uc2 A move above the neckline, $1.1535-$1.1550 would likely see  \par \par \uc2 asharper upside correction, likely toward.... $1.1743. Similar  \par \par \uc2 situation on the downside, a close below the old gap at  \par \par \uc2 $1.1390-$1.1380 would open the target of the double top at  \par \par \uc2 $1.1230-$1.1215."  \par \par \uc2 - DOLLAR/YEN: "The 108.30 yen remains very important on a  \par \par \uc2 weekly close basis. (A double bottom) would only be formed on a  \par \par \uc2 sustained move above the neckline at 111.48 yen, and would  \par \par \uc2 potentially target 115.13 yen. Should be kept in mind that the  \par \par \uc2 Bank of England yen trade weighted index broke to new highs  \par \par \uc2 (above the 2002 highs) yesterday, indicating that on a trade  \par \par \uc2 weighted index basis the yen should remain strong.  \par \par \uc2 - DOLLAR/SWISS FRANC: "The Swiss franc is consolidating  \par \par \uc2 here, a close below 1.3618 francs today would be (the) second  \par \par \uc2 bearish daily reversal in 3 trading days and would be  \par \par \uc2 concerning. The 1.3650 francs to 1.3630 francs remains good  \par \par \uc2 support on closing basis. Below there, at 1.3445 francs.  \par \par \uc2 ANDREW CHAVERIAT, TECHNICAL ANALYST, BNP PARIBAS  \par \par \uc2 - EURO/DOLLAR: "We have got some resistance in the  \par \par \uc2 $1.1535-$1.1545 (area) and there is a good chance to break  \par \par \uc2 that and go up toward $1.1620 and there is some resistance in  \par \par \uc2 $1.1585.  \par \par \uc2 On the downside we have good support, we have hammered out  \par \par \uc2 some lows (at) $1.1455 and $1.1445. The cycle low is $1.1375  \par \par \uc2 doesn't seem in jeopardy at the moment."  \par \par \uc2 - DOLLAR/YEN: "We have got good resistance on the upside  \par \par \uc2 here 109.00-109.10 yen. If we get above there we could see a  \par \par \uc2 pretty good extension toward 109.65 yen and then 110.00 to  \par \par \uc2 110.40 yen. But on the downside we have been holding as there  \par \par \uc2 has been some rumors that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . At the moment we have been holding above  \par \par \uc2 108.50-108.55 yen area. We haven't had much downside excitement  \par \par \uc2 on the trade. Even if we break (below) 108.50 yen we might only  \par \par \uc2 go to 108.30-108.35 yen where we have other support."  \par \par \uc2 DANIEL KATZIVE, \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE\b0 \highlight\uc2  STRATEGIST, UBS:  \par \par \uc2 - EURO/DOLLAR: "It has held in a very tight range either  \par \par \uc2 side of $1.15, and really needs to take out last week's highs  \par \par \uc2 around $1.1540 and, more importantly, technical resistance  \par \par \uc2 around $1.1560 to signify that Friday's bounce has anything  \par \par \uc2 more than short-term significance."  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 10:53 A.M. EST (1553GMT). All data  \par \par \uc2 taken from Reuters calculated from the levels at 4:30 p.m.  \par \par \uc2 (2130 GMT) in the previous New York session.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Last    