\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar jumps as speculation of BOJ action swirls.  \b0\par\par\uc2 618 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2003\par 04:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Reuters offers a scrolling news service for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  professionals who want to follow market developments minute by minute. Click here for the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  news and views  \par \par \uc2 By Mariko Hayashibara  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Nov 11 (Reuters) - The dollar briefly jumped above 109 yen on Tuesday as speculation swirled in the market that the Japanese authorities were \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the yen matched a three-year high against the greenback overnight.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials declined to comment on whether they had stepped in to stem the yen's rise. But market sources said that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York after the dollar retested three-year lows of around 107.85 yen, and started bidding again on Tuesday when the dollar was near 108.65 yen.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback rose as high as 109.09 yen It was trading at 108.75/80 yen at 0316 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 The market has been nervous about possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the dollar fell in a relief rally following the re-election of the coalition government of Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi on the weekend.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is not longer worrying about whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  - everyone expects \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They are just wondering at what level the BOJ will bid," said Takashi Toyahara, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Nomura Securities.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, said on Tuesday he could not comment on whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but said officials would not tolerate excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves.  \par \par \uc2 Echoing Mizoguchi, Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said the authorities would act against sudden movements.  \par \par \uc2 "Judging from the overall trend, last night's moves were rather abrupt," he told a news conference.  \par \par \uc2 "If there are sudden moves that do not reflect fundamentals, we will act as and when needed."  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent a record amount on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the July-September quarter, selling 7.5512 trillion yen, equivalent to $69.4 billion at Tuesday's exchange rate.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this year in an attempt to keep the yen in check and keep alive the country's export-led economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 On September 30, when \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed that it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the New York Federal Reserve, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a massive 1.0667 trillion yen, the fifth-biggest daily amount on record.  \par \par \uc2 "(\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) data released yesterday provided more clear evidence that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the yen's rise," Toyahara said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar/yen was also dragged down by selling in yen cross trade, especially in euro against the yen, with dealers attributing the sales to redemption in euro bonds.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at 124.82/85 yen against 124.89/03 in late U.S. trade, having fallen as low as 124.18 yen on Monday, a 10-month low.  \par \par \uc2 Against the dollar, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at $1.1478/81 versus 1.1470/76.  \par \par \uc2 MACHINERY DATA DUE  \par \par \uc2 Dealers were looking ahead to Japan's September machinery orders data, due at 0500 GMT, for a fresh excuse to bid up the yen.  \par \par \uc2 A Reuters' poll of 28 economists produced a median forecast for a 5.1 percent rise in core orders from the previous month, helped by buoyant exports. Forecasts ranged from a fall of 1.5 percent to a rise of 12.3 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Compared with September last year, orders were seen up a median 7.7 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that the yen could rise on a strong reading.  \par \par \uc2 "Usually, it's rare that the market actively trades on Japanese data, but that is a sign that many people want to create yen long positions now," said a dealer at a Japanese bank. ($1=108.83 yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031111dzbb0014d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
