\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Japanese officials warn against strong yen.  \b0\par\par\uc2 453 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2003\par 03:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 11 (Reuters) - Japanese officials resumed their campaign to talk down the yen on Tuesday after the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose strongly on Monday, reinforcing speculation the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.   \par \par \uc2  The dollar suddenly jumped about a quarter of a yen to about 109.09 yen from about 108.80 in early trading in Tokyo.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials declined to comment on whether they had stepped in to stem the yen's rise.   \par \par \uc2  But market sources said Japanese authorities had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York and started bidding again on Tuesday when the dollar was near 108.65 yen. It was trading around 108.70 at 0210 GMT.   \par \par \uc2  The market has been nervous about possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the dollar retested three-year lows of around 107.85 yen in a relief rally after the re-election on Sunday of the coalition government of Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi.   \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, said on Tuesday he could not comment on whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but said officials would not tolerate excessive moves.   \par \par \uc2  "Excessive volatility and overshooting is not appropriate," he told reporters. "We will act accordingly to such moves."   \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi, vice finance minister for international affairs, said the yen's rise overnight was likely to be temporary.   \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki also said authorities would act against sudden moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.   \par \par \uc2  "Judging from the overall trend, last night's moves were rather abrupt," he told a regular news conference.   \par \par \uc2  "If there are sudden moves that do not reflect fundamentals, we will act as and when needed."   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent a record amount on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the July-September quarter, selling 7.5512 trillion yen, equivalent to $69.4 billion at Tuesday's rate.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this year in an attempt to keep the yen in check and keep alive the country's export-led economic recovery.   \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to fly in the face of a communique issued in September by the Group of Seven industrial nations, which said that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates should be left to the markets.   \par \par \uc2  This was widely seen as a criticism of both Japan and China, whose relatively weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar have been blamed for losses of U.S. manufacturing jobs.   \par \par \uc2  The ministry said its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the G7 meeting - which adopted the communique on September 20 - was on September 30 when it sold a massive 1.0667 trillion yen, the fifth-biggest daily amount on record.   \par \par \uc2  The figure included \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the New York Federal Reserve conducted that day on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behalf. ($1=108.83 yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031111dzbb0004n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
