\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  sold Y7.5512 trln in July-Sept  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 142 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2003\par 00:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Nov 10 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it spent 7.5512 trillion yen ($69.09 billion) on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the July-September quarter to stem the yen's rise.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it stepped into the market on 21 days between July 3 and September 30.  \par \par \uc2 All of the yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in dollar/yen, it said.  \par \par \uc2 The yen's rise, some 6.6 percent against the dollar in July-September, accelerated after a Group of Seven statement called for more flexible exchange rates, which was interpreted as a veiled criticism of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and China.  \par \par \uc2 The ministry has disclosed monthly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amounts until October. In the period from August 28 to September 26, it sold a record 4.4573 trillion yen. ($1=109.28 yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031109dzb900big\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
