\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Japan seen continuing yen sales, US to tolerate.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Charlotte Cooper   \par \uc2 851 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2003\par 16:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 31 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem yen appreciation in October in the face of implicit criticism from its Group of Seven peers but analysts say chief critic Washington is unlikely to gripe louder in coming months.   \par \par \uc2 Data from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  released on Friday showed Japan spent 2.723 trillion yen ($25.04 billion) in October to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from gaining sharply against the dollar and cutting off the country's economic recovery.   \par \par \uc2 This was half the record 4.457 trillion spent in September, the same month a Group of Seven richest nations meeting in Dubai ended in a G7 call for greater \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility - a call the markets read as aimed at Japan and China for keeping their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  down against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 This week, U.S. Secretary John Snow steered clear of outright condemnation of Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, avoiding naming Japan as manipulating the yen for trade gains.   \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will probably continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation as opposed to actively trying to weaken the yen. It seems unlikely at this point in time that we're going to see too much opposition from the U.S. to that policy," said Steven Saywell, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank in London.   \par \par \uc2 "Since Dubai the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amount has dropped to around half the amount in September. But also we have a stronger yen so one way or another Japan has been forced to tolerate a stronger yen."   \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to its lowest level against the yen in three years this week, dropping below 108 yen on Wednesday and shedding six yen since the G7 launched its call. Following Snow's Senate testimony on Thursday it has recovered to 109 yen.   \par \par \uc2 NOT RED OR GREEN BUT AMBER   \par \par \uc2 Asked about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Snow told the Senate Banking Committee he did not want to comment on Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying just that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's attitude was it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent undue \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations.   \par \par \uc2 "We prefer a world of fluctuating rates and we continue to reiterate that," he added.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the mildness of his comments reflected other factors at work, including Japanese elections in November and Japan's pledge of a total $5 billion worth of loans and grants in a U.S.-led drive for aid for Iraq.   \par \par \uc2 "U.S. relations are about a lot of different things at the moment not just \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates," Saywell said.   \par \par \uc2 But Snow was also not giving his blessing to Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.   \par \par \uc2 "I wouldn't say it's a full green light, but what it is saying is that the Americans are not going to increase their pressure any further at this stage on either Japan or China," said Mansoor Mohi-uddin, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS.   \par \par \uc2 DOLLAR'S DIRECTION   \par \par \uc2 Behind the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate is U.S. concern that jobs are being lost through artificially high dollar exchange rates with Asian trading partners, although ire in the U.S. Senate on Thursday was mostly saved for China.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. current account deficit, the broadest measure of U.S. trade with the rest of the world, is on course to top $500 billion this year. While the Bush administration maintains it has a policy of a strong dollar, many in the market believe it wants a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help narrow the current account gap.   \par \par \uc2 But Japan, which has been in an out of recession for a decade, is concerned for its export-led recovery and has sold around 16.2 trillion yen this year to block its rise.   \par \par \uc2 After Snow's soft testimony, analysts say pressure for dollar/yen to fall has abated for now and, with a market heavily long yen and short of dollars, the greenback has scope to rise.   \par \par \uc2 "We're not looking for any further downward pressure in the near-term on dollar/yen. If anything we think it will get a bounce up towards 110," Mohi-uddin said.   \par \par \uc2 But longer term the dollar's downtrend was still in place and even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is thought to be close to its limit on the amount of yen selling it can do this year, analysts expect it will continue reining its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in.   \par \par \uc2 With 10 trillion yen or less left in its 79 trillion \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account to see it through to the end of March, the MOF is expected to raise the ceiling, possibly through an extra budget, to deter any build-up of speculative yen buying pressure.   \par \par \uc2 "The MOF is running out of ammunition and needs to get around this artificial cap to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Steven Pearson, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at HBOS Treasury Services.   \par \par \uc2 MOF sources have indicated one solution could be for the ministry to sell some of its foreign bond holdings to the Bank of Japan under a repurchase agreement to raise extra funds.   \par \par \uc2 "We don't think that is going to be a constraint on future \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said UBS' Mohi-uddin.   \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Burton Frierson and Carolyn Cohn).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031031dzav003bs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
