\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar firm on Snow and U.S. GDP - data ahead.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Burton Frierson  \par \uc2 706 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2003\par 14:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 31 (Reuters) - The dollar rose on Friday, pushing the euro to 10-day lows on upbeat U.S. growth data and after U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow passed up an opportunity to criticise \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 U.S. gross domestic product (GDP) grew at an annual 7.2 percent rate in the third quarter, the fastest pace in nearly two decades and overshooting economists' forecasts. Markets were looking forward to a data-packed U.S. session later on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 In much-awaited testimony to the Senate Banking Committee on Thursday, Snow avoided demanding outright that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  no longer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yen subdued.  \par \par \uc2 "It was definitely a dovish statement. You could say that Snow is not giving a red light to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from yesterday," said Mansoor Mohi-uddin, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS in London.  \par \par \uc2 "We're not looking for any further downward pressure in the near term on dollar/yen. If anything we think it will get a bounce up towards 110."  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was at 109.07 yen at European midsession, up 0.31 percent on the day but still within 1.5 yen of a recent three-year low.  \par \par \uc2 Extending a big fall during New York trade, the euro slipped to a 10-day low of $1.1610 in Asian trade and was at $1.1625.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar showed little reaction to news Japan spent 2.723 trillion yen ($24.96 billion) in preventing its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising on the foreign exchanges in October.  \par \par \uc2 The market had been speculating \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amounted to around one trillion yen in the period, after a year-to-date total of 13.5 trillion yen ($124 billion) up to the end of September.  \par \par \uc2 The yen was also 0.21 percent lower against the euro at 126.74, although still near a recent eight-week high.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. DATA  \par \par \uc2 The focus now switches to U.S. data later in the session after Thursday's GDP surprise provided a strong contrast to Friday's mixed European data.  \par \par \uc2 "Strong data out of the U.S. is giving the dollar very good support from a relative cyclical point of view," said Ian Stannard, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas.  \par \par \uc2 German retail sales stagnated in September, euro zone economic sentiment improved to its highest level in a year in October but the bloc's inflation rate remained stuck above the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's threshold for a third month in a row.  \par \par \uc2 France's jobless rate climbed to its highest level since April 2000, dampening hopes that euro zone's second-largest economy is close to turning the corner.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. data releases due on Friday include personal income and consumption at 1330 GMT and the University of Michigan's consumer sentiment index at 1445 - seen at 89.6 compared with 87.7 in the final September report.  \par \par \uc2 The Chicago Purchasing Managers Index is also due at 1500 GMT and forecast at 55.5 from 51.2 in September.  \par \par \uc2 AFTER SNOW  \par \par \uc2 Snow steered clear of criticising Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Thursday's testimony. The accompanying Treasury report also did not name Japan and China as manipulating their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for trade gains.  \par \par \uc2 Traders thought any such criticism would have made it harder for Tokyo to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively to stem the yen's strength, which it does out of concern that a rise in the yen will squeeze exporters' profits and derail a fragile economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is nearing the ceiling of the yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  it is allowed to undertake, but it is possible it will take steps to increase that limit.  \par \par \uc2 "If we see some movement on that, it could be a catalyst for a nasty squeeze higher in dollar/yen. If there is no change, there is no impediment to dollar/yen going lower," said Steven Pearson, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Halifax Bank of Scotland Treasury Services in London.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan kept monetary policy unchanged at its one-day Policy Board meeting, as expected. Its twice-yearly report, released on Friday, showed the most Policy Board members expect deflation to persist in 2004/05.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031031dzav002xg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
