\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Oct  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  Y2.723 trln yen-MOF.  \b0\par\par\uc2 393 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2003\par 11:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 31 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 2.723 trillion yen ($25.04 billion) in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in October in an effort to prevent the yen from appreciating sharply, \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) data showed on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The October figure showed the Japanese authorities sold that amount in the period from September 27 to October 29, after spending a record 4.4573 trillion yen in September.  \par \par \uc2 During the period, the dollar fell to a new three-year low of 107.86 yen from around 112.25 yen.  \par \par \uc2 On September 30, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) confirmed that it had sold yen for dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, acting through the New York Federal Reserve, breaking its recent silence on market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The disclosure and unusual move through the New York Fed came little more than a week after the Group of Seven industrialised nations called for more flexible exchange rate regimes.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to three-year lows earlier this week on speculation U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow would condemn Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  along with China's dollar-peg for the yuan in his testimony before the Senate Banking Committee on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Traders thought such criticism would have made it harder for Tokyo to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively to stem the yen's strength.  \par \par \uc2 But the greenback recovered the 109 yen level on Friday after Snow steered clear of criticising Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The Treasury Department's report to Congress, which was also released on Thursday, did not name Japan or China as manipulating their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for trade gains.  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese authorities have sold the yen heavily this year to try to stem its rise. They fear a strong yen could hurt exports, hindering the economy's tentative recovery and weakening share prices, which are key to the health of the banking system.  \par \par \uc2 Calculated from both Bank of Japan (BOJ) and MOF data, the September figures lifted this year's total yen selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  volume to around 16.2 trillion yen.  \par \par \uc2 On Friday, BOJ Governor Toshihiko Fukui said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not use its monetary easing policy to guide the yen lower.  \par \par \uc2 He added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not yet received any request from the MOF about possible sales of foreign bonds to boost funds used for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but would consider any such request.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031031dzav002eq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
