\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-MOF Hayashi says Japan has room to act on  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 2003\par 10:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 30 (Reuters) - Japan will continue to act against volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and still has plenty of resources available to do so, Vice Finance Minister Masakazu Hayashi said on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 "The yen's rise since the G7 (in late September) has been sudden," he told reporters at a regular news conference. "As I have said, we will continue to act appropriately against volatility."  \par \par \uc2 "We have plenty of resources available for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said when asked about reports this week that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  may sell some holdings of foreign bonds to the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise cash for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "There is no need to raise extra cash at present," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the ministry to try to curb the yen's strength hit a record 13.5 trillion yen ($124.8 billion) in the first nine months of the year, and the ministry's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  account has come within 12-13 trillion yen of its 79 trillion yen borrowing limit.  \par \par \uc2 The MOF is keen to head off any speculation about a possible fund shortage as it battles to prevent a rise in the yen that it sees as hurting Japan's export-led recovery.  \par \par \uc2 A source told Reuters earlier this week that the ministry will consider necessary measures if markets started to speculate that it might not be able to act because of fund shortages.  \par \par \uc2 Under one possible arrangement, the source said the MOF could sell some of its huge holdings of U.S. Treasury bills and notes - acquired from years of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  - to the BOJ via a repurchase agreement and receive the initial payment in yen.  \par \par \uc2 That would effectively look like a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , buying some time for the MOF if the borrowing ceiling became a serious issue.  \par \par \uc2 However, Hayashi said there has been no specific debate on selling holdings of foreign bonds to the BOJ.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday the yen rose to a three-year high of 107.86 yen to the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031030dzau00260\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
