\par\par \b \uc2 Yen touches 3-yr high on dlr, US-Asia debate eyed.  \b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 2003\par 09:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 29 (Reuters) - The yen hit a three-year high on the dollar and the greenback fell against the euro on Wednesday as strong Japanese output data fanned expectations Washington would criticise Asia nations' \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies later this week.  \par \par \uc2 A Federal Reserve decision to leave rates steady on Tuesday was no surprise but the wording of its statement disappointed those who had looked for hints as to when the U.S. recovery might be strong enough to warrant an upward tweak in interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 "The immediate impact is slightly negative for the dollar," said Aziz McMahon, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro.  \par \par \uc2 "It seems policy is to remain accommodative for longer than people thought...It's a slight disappointment for the dollar near term but it suggests things are getting better."  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb dollar weakness against the yen as Asian trade got underway.  \par \par \uc2 Nevertheless the dollar fell to 107.97 yen in late Asian trade, after Japanese output data showed a rise of 3.0 percent in September, the biggest rise since May 2002 and higher than forecast.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By 0755 GMT the dollar was back at 108.00 yen, off a quarter percent on\par the day. The euro was half a percent up at $1.1715  and a quarter\par percent higher on the yen at 126.78 yen           after falling sharply\par in recent days.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Eyes now are on U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow's congressional testimony on Asian nations' \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy due on Thursday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Before that however, the Norwegian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meets to decided on interest rates later on Wednesday. No change is expected.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dallas Fed President Robert McTeer speaks later in the session and Richmond Fed President Alfred Broaddus also speaks at 1345 GMT.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031029dzat00176\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
