\par\par \b \uc2 Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Up Late; Yen's 3-Yr High Lifts Regionals  \b0\par\par\uc2 981 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 2003\par 10:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened across the board Wednesday, helped by the yen's rise to a three-year high against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 In addition to the yen's updraft, the South Korean won benefited from unexpectedly strong economic data, raising hopes the country is pulling out of its first recession since the late-1990s regional financial crisis.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell below Y108 for the first time since November 2000 as data out of Japan pointed to a continued recovery in the world's second-largest economy and after the Federal Reserve left U.S. interest rates unchanged overnight.  \par \par \uc2 In the latest in a string of encouraging economic reports, the Japanese government said industrial production expanded a stronger-than-expected 3.0% in September from August.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar changed hands as low as Y107.86 late in the Asia session, despite dollar bids just above the Y108 level, which several dealers suspected were placed on behalf of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The ministry has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets this year trying to curb the yen's strength, selling a record 13.5 trillion yen through September to support the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Boosted by good economic news at home as well as the yen's strength, the won posted its best performance in more than a week, pushing the dollar down to close at KRW1,178.3 from KRW1,183.3 a day earlier.  \par \par \uc2 Korea's manufacturing sector grew by 6.6% in September from a year ago, while the current-account surplus for the month widened to its largest gap in more than four years, the government said.  \par \par \uc2 With exports likely to remain robust, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is predicting the current-account surplus will swell to $10 billion this year, far more than the $2 billion it estimated earlier in the year.  \par \par \uc2 "These data indicate room for a downside in dollar/won, especially if the current account moves in like with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest expectations," Bank of America said in a research note.  \par \par \uc2 In addition, the won was underpinned by foreign money flowing into the local stock market and heavy dollar selling by local exporters.  \par \par \uc2 In Singapore, the yen's rise prompted domestic banks to trim their U.S. dollar position in favor of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 In late Asian trading the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7375, down from S$1.7440 late Tuesday in Asia.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar opened near its session high of S$1.74505, but quickly began a slide that progressed through the rest of the trading day.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the Fed's decision to keep U.S. short-term interest rates unchanged at a 45-year low also damped appetite for U.S. dollars.  \par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah rebounded from a 12-week low to finish the Asian session stronger as the government's sale of two major banking assets helped restore confidence in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Near the end of Asian trading the dollar was quoted at IDR8,530, down from IDR8,585 Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar rose to IDR8,600 in early trading as investors dumped the rupiah due to concerns over a probe into an alleged $200 million lending scandal involving Bank Negara Indonesia.  \par \par \uc2 However, the local unit began recovering after the government announced it had raised about $490 million from the sale of a 40.5% stake in state-owned PT Bank Rakyat Indonesia. The sale was the largest IPO by an Indonesian company since the 1997-98 Asian financial crisis.  \par \par \uc2 Later, the Indonesian Bank Restructuring Agency announced the sale of a 51% stake in PT Bank Internasional Indonesia to a consortium led by South Korea's Kookmin Bank and Temasek Holdings Pte. Ltd., the Singapore government's investment arm.  \par \par \uc2 IBRA didn't disclose the exact financial terms of the deal, but analysts said the deal would raise around $200 million for the government, which also boosted market sentiment.  \par \par \uc2 The New Taiwan dollar benefited from the yen's rise, as well as usual month-end demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from exporters.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar closed at NT$33.945, lower than NT$33.988 Tuesday. Dealings were valued at US$437 million, up from US$404 million Tuesday. The U.S. dollar fell below the NT$33.95 support level in line with the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's breaching of the Y108 mark.  \par \par \uc2 Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the New Taiwan dollar's appreciation, stayed out of the market because the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise was in line with its regional peers.  \par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso strengthened for the second straight day as jitters over political developments continued to ease.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at PHP55.24 on the Philippine Dealing System, down from its PHP55.35 close in the previous session.  \par \par \uc2 Already battered in recent months by an attempted army mutiny, the attempted suspension of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor and concerns over next year's presidential election, the peso had sunk to a record low Monday on concerns that an impeachment complaint filed by lawmakers against the country's Supreme Court chief justice would result in a political stalemate.  \par \par \uc2 However, hopes for a settlement were raised Tuesday when congressional leaders adjourned the legislative session until Nov. 10, giving President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo time to broker a possible compromise.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Rafael Buenaventura said with corporate demand for the dollar satisfied and "political noise" subsiding, the pressure on the peso has eased and the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could still strengthen to 54 per dollar by year-end.  \par \par \uc2 Against the Thai baht, the dollar was quoted at THB39.925 in late Asian trading, down fractionally from THB39.935 late Tuesday in Asia.  \par \par \uc2 -By Alan Yonan Jr., Dow Jones Newswires; 65 9862-0905; alan.yonan@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 1136 4250  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031029dzat000i8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
