\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Slips To New Multi-Yr Lows Vs Yen, Pound  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Jonathan Soble  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 797 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 2003\par 06:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar slipped to a fresh three-year low against the yen in Asia Wednesday, but stuck to a tight range amid rumors that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities were quietly supporting the U.S. unit.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar also lost ground against its European counterparts, falling to a new five-year low against the British pound after the U.S. federal reserve's decision Tuesday to keep interest rates steady at 45-year lows.  \par \par \uc2 "There's still a feeling in the market that the dollar's downside hasn't been fully tested," said a senior dealer at one of Japan's big four banks. "People are still eager to try pushing it lower across a whole range of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the dollar fell as low as Y108.09, coming within a stroke of its first break below Y108 since Nov. 14, 2000. Data showing unexpectedly strong growth in Japanese industrial production in September helped drag the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower.  \par \par \uc2 Several dealers noted a series of small-lot dollar bids by Japanese banks just above Y108, which they suspected were placed on behalf of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The MOF spent some Y13.5 trillion in the first nine months of the year to keep a lid on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "You don't get the impression that they are trying aggressively to push the dollar up," said Satoshi Tate, a vice president for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at UFJ Bank. "It's more like an effort to smooth its fall. The bid amounts are quite small."  \par \par \uc2 Action in the options market also helped support the dollar, dealers said. An Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was said to be defending $1 billion worth options, due to expire Thursday, that would be void if the dollar fell to Y108.00.  \par \par \uc2 Industrial production in Japan surged 3.0% in September from August, beating economists' average forecast for a 1.5% rise as strong demand for exports flowed through to domestic manufacturers.  \par \par \uc2 "The lift in momentum is consistent with other economic data, and confirms that export growth is finally being felt in domestic manufacturing activity," said Ryo Hino, an economist at J.P. Morgan.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y108.09, below Y108.32 late Tuesday in New York. The dollar was at Y108.25 late Tuesday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.1686, higher than $1.1662 late Tuesday in New York. The euro was at $1.1707 in Tokyo Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y126.35, up marginally from Y126.32 in New York late Tuesday. The euro was at Y126.73 in Tokyo late Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.7008, off its peak of 1.7019 but higher than $1.6977 in New York. Sterling was at $1.6917 in Tokyo Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The euro got a reprieve from its recent slide against the yen after the end of a series of euro-denominated bond redemptions, which dealers say had weighed on the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since late last week.  \par \par \uc2 "Now we could see a rebound (for the euro) in the next few days as Japanese investors put their money back into new euro-denominated assets," said the head dealer at a European brokerage in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 For the dollar, a key test is set to come Thursday with U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow's Congressional testimony on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which coincides with the release of the Treasury Department's semiannual report on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "There's a real risk that the dollar could dive" against the yen, said UFJ's Tate. "The report might not mention Japan by name, but it's sure to be critical of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies in general."  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. has been urging China, in particular, to allow more flexibility in the value of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , now pegged to the dollar. U.S. manufacturers, and some members of Congress who represent them, complain that China is keeping its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  undervalued to cheapen its exports.  \par \par \uc2 Those same complaints also extend to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the rise in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - thus U.S. pressure on China to let the yuan strengthen also tends to boost the yen.  \par \par \uc2 -By Jonathan Soble, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; jonathan.soble@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Bennett Richardson and Hugh Lawson  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX  \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031029dzat00069\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscale