\par\par \b \uc2 BC-MARKETS-JAPAN- \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY \highlight\uc2  (REFILES).   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Hideyuki Sano   \par \uc2 633 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2003\par 04:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Repeating to South Asian services)   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 28 (Reuters) - The dollar hit a new three-year low against the yen on Tuesday amid speculation that U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow could condemn Japan's attempts to weaken the yen at a Senate hearing later this week.   \par \par \uc2 Speculation that Washington might take such action, fuelled by a Group of Seven (G7) statement on September 20 calling for flexible exchange rates, was reignited when Snow said on Monday he had reiterated to China the need for more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates.   \par \par \uc2 In addition, downward momentum on the dollar was increasing. It has been unable over the last few weeks to sustain a bounce above the psychological 110 yen threshold, prompting Japanese exporters and investors to give up on their strategy of waiting for a significant rebound before selling dollars.   \par \par \uc2 "What was initially speculation about U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy after G7 and an inflow of foreign investment flows into the Tokyo stock market is turning into a broader move," said Mitsuru Sahara, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at UFJ Bank.   \par \par \uc2 "Exporters are lowering the levels for their dollar-selling orders and Japanese investors are starting to repatriate some of their foreign bond holdings," he said.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar hit a three-year low of 108.20 yen in early Tokyo trade. At 0225 GMT, it stood at 108.35/40 yen , down marginally from Monday's late New York levels.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said yen buying was heavier against the euro, which fell to around 126.80 yen from around 127.40 yen in late U.S. trade.   \par \par \uc2 The euro also slipped to $1.1715 , versus $1.1750 late on Monday. Traders said the euro was sold for profit-taking after the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to rise beyond recent highs on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 SNOW TESTIMONY   \par \par \uc2 Traders said wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities, who have made no secret of their concern that the yen's strength could choke off the nation's export-led economic recovery, was putting a brake on the dollar's decline for now.   \par \par \uc2 "I think they are likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the dollar falls further," said Seiya Nakajima, chief economist at Itochu Corp.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the biggest focus in the market was Snow's testimony at a Senate hearing on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies scheduled for Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 He recently repeated the long-standing U.S. Treasury mantra that a strong dollar is in U.S. interest and that exchange rates are determined by the market. Even so, many doubt he is committed to keeping the dollar strong.   \par \par \uc2 "It's pretty obvious the U.S. government wants a cheaper dollar," said Nakajima of Itochu Corp.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said senators would likely press him to elaborate on his - and the G7's - remarks on "flexible" exchange rates, which have been interpreted in the market as a criticism against the Chinese yuan's virtual peg against the dollar and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold down the yen.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amounting to a record 13.5 trillion yen ($124.5 billion) in just the first nine months of the year. It is due to unveil its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  figures for October on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 Most of the scheduled events before Snow's testimony were expected to receive only muted reaction, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 While third-quarter U.S. gross domestic product figures on Wednesday were forecast to show strong growth of around six percent on an annualised basis, traders said the market had already largely discounted such numbers.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. Federal Reserve's rate-setting Federal Open Market Committee meeting on Tuesday was not expected to change monetary policy, although the market will closely scrutinise any statement by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for hints about its future policy. ($1=108.43 yen).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031028dzas000pz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
