\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Japan \highlight\uc2  Can  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2 , But Will It?  \b0\par\par\uc2 516 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2003\par 07:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 Fukui's apparent reference to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  followed a report in this morning's Nihon Keizai Shimbun - which was first released overnight in New York - that Japan's finance ministry and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  were hammering out a proposal for the government to sell a portion of its roughly Y50 trillion of U.S. Treasurys and other foreign bond holdings in order to overcome any possible funding shortage to finance more yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Japanese financial authorities "used to be reluctant to disclose this kind of information, but markets are now focusing on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy," said Tomoko Fujii, head of economic and market analysis at Nikko Citigroup. "This is a very strong message that there's no practical limit on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The authorities probably thought it would be helpful to emphasize they aren't retreating."  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have insisted that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy remains unchanged and that they will take action in markets as needed. But after selling a record amount of yen this year, they've apparently backed off since mid-September, after the Group of Seven industrial powers called for more flexible exchange rates.  \par \par \uc2 The Nikkei report demonstrates how Japan could continue its policy of stemming the yen's rise if authorities wanted to do so, but Tuesday's fresh low prompted market participants to question whether or not Japan would step in any time soon to stem the dollar's slide.  \par \par \uc2 While the pair remained above the key technical level of Y108.00, which is also a formidable options barrier, many traders wondered how long that level would hold as options positions expired.  \par \par \uc2 The performance of Japanese equities will partly determine the extent of downward pressure on the dollar in the coming weeks and months, Fujii said.  \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the Nikkei 225 Stock Average recouped some of its recent losses, closing up 1.0% at 10561.01. But Tokyo Stock Exchange First Section volume was below 1 billion shares for the second consecutive session, which could be a sign that foreign investor interest is waning.  \par \par \uc2 "We still don't see outflows at this time, but at least we can see a clear deceleration of foreign buying," Fujii said.  \par \par \uc2 European buying of Japanese equities boosted the yen against the euro in August, but such buying has now tapered off, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The euro spent most of Tuesday's Asian session trading under Y127.00, and at one point fell to a two-week low of Y126.69.  \par \par \uc2 Against the dollar, the euro traded in a narrow band between $1.1705 and $1.1751 in Asia.  \par \par \uc2 -By Lisa Twaronite, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; lisa.twaronite@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Bennett Richardson  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031028dzas0009w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
