\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Edges Down To New 3-Year Low Vs Yen  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Lisa Twaronite  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 881 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2003\par 06:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar fell to a new three-year low against the yen in Asia Tuesday, as Japanese exporters sold the pair and U.S. and European funds also tested the downside.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar peaked early, getting no higher than Y108.55 at 2132 GMT. It then drifted lower and touched Y108.20 on the EBS system late in the morning session. This marked its lowest point since November 2000, beating the old low of Y108.27 hit overnight.  \par \par \uc2 But given Tuesday's extremely narrow trading range, this morning's low didn't alarm market participants, as many believed it was just a continuation of the dollar's recent weakness rather than a sudden downside break, said Toshihiko Masaki, Tokyo branch treasurer at China Construction Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "The pair's fall this morning was gradual, not sudden, meaning it was likely the result of position adjustments rather than a big trend move," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar remained under pressure in the afternoon session, despite an oblique warning about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Toshihiko Fukui.  \par \par \uc2 Fukui said after a speech to business leaders that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates have been volatile as market participants worry that the U.S.' twin deficits could undermine a global economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 "This has naturally caused irregular movements" in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, Fukui said, adding authorities would have to carry out "appropriate financial \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 " - an apparent allusion to yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although he didn't specify any particular action.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not the Bank of Japan, makes Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, so market participants didn't take Fukui's comments as a precursor of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y108.25, below Y108.57 in both New York and Tokyo late Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.1707, lower than $1.1747 in New York and $1.1732 in Tokyo. Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y126.73, compared with Y127.52 in New York and Y127.43 in Tokyo Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.6917, compared with $1.6946 in New York and $1.6924 in Tokyo Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Fukui's apparent reference to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  followed a report in this morning's Nihon Keizai Shimbun - which was first released overnight in New York - that Japan's finance ministry and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  were hammering out a proposal for the government to sell a portion of its roughly Y50 trillion of U.S. Treasurys and other foreign bond holdings in order to overcome any possible funding shortage to finance more yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Japanese financial authorities "used to be reluctant to disclose this kind of information, but markets are now focusing on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy," said Tomoko Fujii, head of economic and market analysis at Nikko Citigroup. "This is a very strong message that there's no practical limit on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The authorities probably thought it would be helpful to emphasize they aren't retreating."  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have insisted that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy remains unchanged and that they will take action in markets as needed. But after selling a record amount of yen this year, they've apparently backed off since mid-September, after the Group of Seven industrial powers called for more flexible exchange rates.  \par \par \uc2 The Nikkei report demonstrates how Japan could continue its policy of stemming the yen's rise if authorities wanted to do so, but Tuesday's fresh low prompted market participants to question whether or not Japan would step in any time soon to stem the dollar's slide.  \par \par \uc2 While the pair remained above the key technical level of Y108.00, which is also a formidable options barrier, many traders wondered how long that level would hold as options positions expired.  \par \par \uc2 The performance of Japanese equities will partly determine the extent of downward pressure on the dollar in the coming weeks and months, Fujii said.  \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the Nikkei 225 Stock Average recouped some of its recent losses, closing up 1.0% at 10561.01. But Tokyo Stock Exchange First Section volume was below 1 billion shares for the second consecutive session, which could be a sign that foreign investor interest is waning.  \par \par \uc2 "We still don't see outflows at this time, but at least we can see a clear deceleration of foreign buying," Fujii said.  \par \par \uc2 European buying of Japanese equities boosted the yen against the euro in August, but such buying has now tapered off, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The euro spent most of Tuesday's Asian session trading under Y127.00, and at one point fell to a two-week low of Y126.69.  \par \par \uc2 Against the dollar, the euro traded in a narrow band between $1.1705 and $1.1751 in Asia.  \par \par \uc2 -By Lisa Twaronite, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; lisa.twaronite@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Bennett Richardson  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX  \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031028dzas0006x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
