\par\par \b \uc2 Takenaka: Ctrl Bk, Govt Cooperating To Beat Deflation -FT  \b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Oktober 2003\par 00:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Japan's economy minister, Heizo Takenaka, said in an interview that the country could overcome deflation because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was working more closely with the government, The Financial Times reported on its Web site Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Takenaka said the Bank of Japan would aim to raise money supply growth rate to between 3% and 4% its current level of 2%, the report said.  \par \par \uc2 The government, he said, would increase demand through deregulation and would also clean up the banking system so that the BOJ's looser monetary policy would be transmitted to the economy as a whole, according the report.  \par \par \uc2 "By combining these two our calculations say we will be able to overcome deflation," Takenaka was quoted by the FT as saying.  \par \par \uc2 Takenaka praised BOJ Governor Toshihiko Fukui, suggesting that he was more determined than his predecessor to halt deflation."Since Governor Fukui took office, BOJ policy is, in my opinion, moving in a good direction," he was quoted as saying.  \par \par \uc2 Takenaka said that, "even with the Consumer Price Index nearing zero," the BOJ had signaled its commitment to easy monetary policy for as long as necessary, according to the report.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ was "contemplating right now" how to signal its long-term commitment to price stability, with some BOJ members advocating a reference rate, a goal just short of an inflation target, he said, according to the FT.  \par \par \uc2 Takenaka played down suggestions that U.S. President George W. Bush will use Friday's meeting with Japanese Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi to urge an end to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. "The summit meeting is not a venue at which \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy should be discussed," he was quoted as saying.  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031016dzag00159\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
