\par\par \b \uc2 Japan Tanigaki: Don't See Change To US Strong Dlr Policy  \b0\par\par\uc2 665 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2003\par 10:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to correct irregular \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market movements has the understanding of the international community, including the U.S., which still supports a stronger dollar, Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said Wednesday  \par \par \uc2 "Listening to what U.S. officials have been saying, it seems their stance to sustain a strong dollar appears to be unchanged," Tanigaki told reporters, when asked about recent remarks by U.S. President George W. Bush.  \par \par \uc2 Speaking ahead of a trip to Tokyo Friday, Bush said yesterday: "We expect the markets to reflect the true value of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a remark which has been interpreted as a clear indication that he intends to raise the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's persistent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yen from strengthening.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki added that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  also maintains that, as a rule, exchange rates are decided by the markets and should move stably in reflection of fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 But if movements become speculative or irregular, Japan will take necessary action to smooth such moves, Tanigaki said.  \par \par \uc2 "This is a stance which is internationally understood," he said, brushing aside speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be pressured to scale back \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki appeared to be trying to downplay speculation that Bush will use his visit to Tokyo to pressure \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depress the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Market players believe that Bush's government, heading into an election year, has taken up the banner of U.S. manufacturers who accuse Asian countries of keeping their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  - and thus their exports - artificially cheap, undercutting U.S. products and stealing American jobs.  \par \par \uc2 But Tanigaki said that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which the authorities claim are aimed at curbing excessive volatility, have been acknowledged by the Group of Seven industrialized nations.  \par \par \uc2 "The G7 expressed that in Dubai," Tanigaki said, referring to the communique released after finance ministers and central bankers from the world's richest nations met in Dubai last month. In the comminuque, the G7 said they would monitor markets and "cooperate" as needed.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki also brushed aside market speculation that Japan's Finance Ministry may soon hit a ceiling on government borrowing to finance \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "At the moment, our \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds are not running dry," Tanigaki said.  \par \par \uc2 Recent media reports have said the ministry is planning to raise the ceiling for government borrowing to finance \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Y10 trillion-Y20 trillion from the current Y79 trillion.  \par \par \uc2 With the government having sold more than Y10 trillion this year, concerns are emerging that the ceiling could be hit if the massive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  continue.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki also shot down speculation that the Finance Ministry may ask the Bank of Japan to buy foreign bonds held by the government to provide extra funds for possible future \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "While I am aware of such debate, I don't think that will happen at the moment," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki said, however, he believes more monetary policy easing is needed to support the economy.  \par \par \uc2 "Although this is not directly related to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I think there is a need for continued quantitative monetary policy easing," Tanigaki said, adding he welcomed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent decision to ease policy further.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ's policy board Friday decided to increase the upper end of the account balance target by Y2 trillion to Y32 trillion, leaving the bottom of the target unchanged at Y27 trillion.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki also said that the government will aim to finance its planned $1.5 billion contribution for the reconstruction of Iraq through its budget for official development assistance.  \par \par \uc2 The government announced earlier Wednesday it will contribute the funds, which will go toward electricity, education, water and health support.  \par \par \uc2 "We aren't thinking of one yet," Tanigaki said, when asked if the government may compile an extra budget in the event it needs more funding to provide the support.  \par \par \uc2 -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031015dzaf000ie\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
