\par\par \b \uc2 Tokyo Shares End Higher On Hopes For Good 1H Corp Results  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Michele Yamada  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 884 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2003\par 08:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Asian Equities Report\par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Tokyo stocks rose Tuesday as gains on Wall Street overnight cheered sentiment among investors here on the prospects for upcoming corporate earnings results, encouraging many to snap up shares of big banks and high tech exporters like Advantest.  \par \par \uc2 The Nikkei 225 Stock Average rose 180.39 points, or 1.7%, to end at 10966.43 after gaining 254.60 points Friday. The market was closed Monday for a public holiday.  \par \par \uc2 "The market trend has been quite firm," said Seiki Orimi, chief strategist at UFJ Tsubasa Securities. "Strong third-quarter earnings from the U.S. are showing the positive impact of President Bush's tax cut, and investors are now feeling relieved on the employment figures there."  \par \par \uc2 Amid such prospects for a global market recovery, "many players are also feeling more at ease about buying Japan shares," he added.  \par \par \uc2 Ahead of U.S. chip giant Intel's earnings, which are due later in the global day and expected to be firm, players rushed to buy chip-related issues such as Tokyo Electron and Advantest.  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo Electron, the world's second-largest manufacturer of chip-making equipment, also attracted buying after the company Friday upgraded its earnings outlook for the six months ended September 30 due to stronger-than-expected orders on increased capital spending by chip makers. The issue ended up 5.9% at Y8,040.  \par \par \uc2 Gains in other chip-related shares helped the index top 11000 in the morning. Customized chipmaker Rohm rose 5.1% to Y14,390, while NEC Electronics advanced 2.7% to Y8,320.  \par \par \uc2 The Topix index of all the Tokyo Stock Exchange First Section issues rose 13.43 points, or 1.3%, to 1087.31, a fresh year-high on a closing basis, thanks to strong buying of big banks, especially by pension funds and investment trusts that are building new index-linked products, a local trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Mitsubishi Tokyo Financial Group gained 5.9% to Y919,000, while Resona Holdings jumped 8.2% to Y185 following its Friday announcement of steps to clean up its balance sheet.  \par \par \uc2 After topping the 11000 mark midmorning, the Nikkei turned dull, hovering just above 10900 for most of the afternoon. But buying by foreign investors, particularly Europeans, pushed the index higher late in the session.  \par \par \uc2 Players said resistance at 11000 still looks hard to break, especially as investors may become increasingly cautious as the reporting season begins for corporate earnings for Japan's first fiscal half.  \par \par \uc2 The yen's strength may also weigh on the index, especially as many in the market expect \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold off from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to weaken the yen against the dollar ahead of U.S. President George W. Bush's visit to Tokyo later this week.  \par \par \uc2 Although strong earnings results from U.S. companies such as Motorola or Intel may make it easier for Tokyo investors to buy, "such U.S.-driven gains on Nikkei usually won't last toward the end of each session. You want to take profits," said a local trader.  \par \par \uc2 Many traders predict such market conditions will keep the Nikkei in a range of 10100-11500.  \par \par \uc2 On the broader TSE First Section, 697 issues rose, 716 fell, and 113 ended flat. Volume was estimated at about 1.44 billion shares, down from 1.58 billion shares Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Although some pessimists raised concerns about the sustainability of a U.S. market recovery beyond October, brisk buying of high-tech blue chips and banks pushed the market capitalization of the First Section to its highest level so far this year of about Y318.15 trillion.  \par \par \uc2 The appetite of individuals and foreign investors continued to be strong. Softbank jumped 11% to Y5,970 on buying by individual investors.  \par \par \uc2 The near-term December Nikkei 225 futures contract ended just shy of 11000, up 220 points at 10980 on the Osaka Securities Exchange.  \par \par \uc2 Auto shares ended mixed. Nissan Motor rose 1.2% to Y1.250, while Toyota Motor added 1.2% to Y3,450. Mazda Motor slid 0.4% to Y279, and Suzuki Motor fell 1.1% to Y1,697.  \par \par \uc2 Video game maker Konami surged 9.3% to Y3,870 after the company said it aims to increase its global market share by expanding its \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to Los Angeles and strengthening its content planning and production business.  \par \par \uc2 Among decliners, printer maker Seiko Epson shed 0.6% to Y3,580, retailer Ito-Yokado fell 2.7% to Y4,340. Japan Telecom lost 2.6% to end at Y370,000.  \par \par \uc2 Brokerages shares ended higher. Nomura Holdings rose 1.2% to Y1,902, while Shinko Securities advanced 7.9% to Y370.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                            Close    Previous   Change \par                                        Close \par Nikkei 225 Stock Avg    10966.43    10786.04   +180.39 \par Nikkei 300                211.23      208.52     +2.71 \par Topix Index              1087.31     1073.88    +13.43 \par First Section Volume      1.44 bln    1.58 bln \par Second Section Average   2212.68     2187.64    +25.04 \par Second Section Volume    40.58 mln   42.82 mln \par Nikkei Jasdaq Stk Avg    1436.76     1407.19    +29.57 \par  \par    -By Michele Yamada, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2955; Michele.Yamada@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie  \f28 \par \par \uc2 4159 5011 55117  \par \par \uc2 Dokument AER0000020031014dzae0000e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
