\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar pares gains as U.S. equities lose momentum.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By John Parry  \par \uc2 571 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2003\par 18:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Oct 14 (Reuters) - The dollar shed much of its earlier broad gains on Tuesday after U.S. stock markets inched down from their highest levels in over a year, removing some of the impetus behind the dollar rally.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier in Tuesday's global session, the dollar had rallied across the board, hitting one-week highs against the euro and the yen, as U.S. earnings optimism prompted a rebound in the greenback after seven straight weeks of decline.  \par \par \uc2 "We had a pretty good equity market rally yesterday, because decent earnings reports came out, but that is just pausing now.... We have had some profit taking (in dollars)" said Grant Wilson, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with Mellon Bank in Pittsburgh, Penn.  \par \par \uc2 In late morning New York trade, the euro was flat on the day at $1.1706. The dollar maintained gains against the yen, trading at 109.37 yen, up 0.4 percent on the day, but off session highs of 110.25 yen. The dollar slipped to 1.3209 Swiss francs, down 0.1 percent on the day.  \par \par \uc2 The pound rose to $1.6686, up 0.2 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier in the session, after weeks of concentrating on the U.S. current account deficit and the need for a weaker dollar to correct it, investors switched focus to the brighter outlook for corporate America as Bank of America and Merrill Lynch posted encouraging results.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback leaped more than 1 percent to its session highs against the yen, as speculative traders scrambled to exit long yen/short dollar positions.  \par \par \uc2 ONE EYE ON BOJ  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the dollar was also helped by talk that Japan was still selling yen to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent export-hurting appreciation. Japan has already thrown more than 13.5 trillion yen at the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this year in a bid to slow the yen's rise.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the market remains nervous about the possibility that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could step in with further yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Traders noted there was continued uncertainty about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy ahead of U.S. President George W. Bush's visit to Japan on Friday. Bush is expected to discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when he meets Japanese Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi.  \par \par \uc2 Among Federal Reserve officials' remarks on Tuesday, Fed Governor Ben Bernanke told the Senate Banking Committee that the Fed sees risks that already low inflation could drift lower, putting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a position to hold interest rates at a low level to foster a sustained recovery in the long-suffering U.S. jobs market.  \par \par \uc2 Fed officials "are pretty consistent that we will keep the pedal (of low interest rates) to the metal until we see a dramatic growth in employment," said Wilson of Mellon Bank.  \par \par \uc2 In Europe, an unexpected fall in German economic sentiment in October had little impact on the euro, with many analysts noting that weak data tends to support bond markets, which in turn support the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The ZEW index fell 0.6 points to 60.3, marking its first drop in 10 months.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's recovery started on Monday after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg said a call by the Group of Seven major industrialized nations last month for exchange rate flexibility was not directed at the euro. (Additional reporting by Christina Fincher in London).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031014dzae002g9\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cel